\paragraph{Intervention resistance.}
Seven targeted interventions across four levels fail to reliably eliminate CIVO (Table~\ref{tab:intervention_hierarchy}): gradient stopping shifts co-adaptation to unblocked pathways, output capping (RAVE) is defeated by its own EMA anchor tracking biased values, and representation noise (TCN) gates rather than attenuates the pathology with effective dosage that does not transfer across environments. The pattern indicates pathway redundancy---CIVO exploits whichever gradient channel remains open---consistent with it being a systemic property of imagination-based training with temporal conditioning rather than a defect in any single component.

